  "steps": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "Place the Pico with power disconnected",
      "text": "Keep USB and battery disconnected. USB socket at top; insert all left header pins in c3-c22 and right pins in h3-h22. Leave the side rails unused."
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "title": "Build the Pico supply branch",
      "text": "D1 anode a30, striped cathode a35. J1 b35 to j4 (VSYS); J2 b50 to j5 (GND). L1 b30 to external P5V; L2 a50 to external PGND. Leave L1/L2 disconnected at source until voltage checks. VBUS h3 is unused."
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "title": "Add first servo signal",
      "text": "R_PWM0 f30 to f35, J3 j22 to j30, L3 j35 to servo 0 signal. Servo power and ground connect directly to external P5V and PGND."
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "title": "Optional second servo",
      "text": "For two servos add R_PWM1 f40 to f45, J4 j21 to j40, L4 j45 to servo 1 signal. Add its external power and ground leads. Omit these for one servo."
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "title": "Inspect and measure before connecting electronics",
      "text": "Check every connection unpowered. Remove Pico and unplug servos, then connect the supply branch and switch on for voltage checks. Black meter probe c50 (GND); red c30 (regulated 5V), then c35 (after D1, below 5.5V). Disconnect battery before reinstalling Pico and connecting one unloaded servo. This diagram is not proof of powered operation."
    }
  ],
